/target

# Deck files are the one thing that lands in the working tree just by using
# the tool: `manaline deck new <name>` writes `<name>.txt` into the current
# directory, and `deck edit` creates its file if it does not exist. So decks
# are ignored by default and the starter decks are allowed back in by name.

# Local decks written at the repo root.
/*.txt

# Everything in decks/ except the starter decks. The code treats every deck
# in that directory alike and reads them at run time, so this list is the
# only thing that makes a deck a "starter" one: it is what a fresh clone has.
/decks/*
!/decks/white.txt
!/decks/blue.txt
!/decks/black.txt
!/decks/red.txt
!/decks/green.txt
!/decks/wu-fliers.txt
!/decks/ub-control.txt
!/decks/br-goblins.txt
!/decks/rg-stompy.txt
!/decks/gw-elves.txt
!/decks/wb-lifegain.txt
